\newlabel{fig:data_efficiency}{{5}{7}{Data efficiency of equivariant networks. Force prediction error vs.\ training set size for water molecules. $L=0$ uses only scalars (invariant); $L \geq 1$ includes vector and higher-order equivariant features. Equivariant networks achieve lower error at all training set sizes. Figure from~\cite {batzner2022nequip}}{figure.5}{}}
